  "result": "Excellent! All 173 tests pass. Here's a summary of the voucher implementation:\n\n## Summary\n\n\u2705 **Added `applyVoucher(invoice, { code, amount })` function to `src/invoices.js`:**\n- Takes a fixed amount in cents off the invoice, applied after VAT\n- Returns `ok(newInvoice)` with `invoice.voucher = { code, amount }`\n- Only for draft invoices (error: `NOT_DRAFT`)\n- Amount must be a positive integer in cents (error: `AMOUNT_INVALID`)\n- Only one voucher per invoice (error: `VOUCHER_EXISTS`)\n- Preserves immutability\n\n\u2705 **Updated `invoiceTotals()` function:**\n- Now returns `voucher` amount (0 if no voucher applied)\n- Calculates total correctly: `total = subtotal - discount + vat - voucher`\n- Clamps total to 0 (never negative)\n\n\u2705 **Preserved voucher across all operations:**\n- `addLine()` preserves voucher when modifying draft invoices\n- `removeLine()` preserves voucher when modifying draft invoices\n- `issueInvoice()` preserves voucher when issuing\n- `recordPayment()` preserves voucher when recording payments\n\n\u2705 **Added `VOUCHER_EXISTS` error code** to `src/errors.js`\n\n\u2705 **Added 9 comprehensive tests** to `test/invoices.test.js`:\n- Applying vouchers to draft invoices\n- Error handling for non-draft invoices\n- Error handling for duplicate vouchers\n- Error handling for invalid amounts\n- Voucher included in total calculations\n- Voucher preservation through addLine, removeLine, and issueInvoice\n- Proper handling when no voucher is applied\n\nAll 173 tests pass.",
